'''Corporació de Plàstics Jala, S.A.''' ({{lang|ca|Corporació de Plàstics Jala}}), commonly known as '''Jala Plastics''' or '''CPJ''', is a Balboan {{w|engineering plastics}} company specialising in high-performance polymers, including '''PEEK''', '''PAI''', '''PBI''', '''ECTFE''', '''PI''', and '''PTFE'''. Headquartered in Zone 2, [[Sant Bart]], the company operates a vertically integrated production complex in [[Jala]] province and is one of the leading domestic suppliers of advanced plastics for aerospace, electronics, chemical processing, and industrial applications. The Jala name refers to the province and industrial district, not to the founder's family.

CPJ is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] (SCX: CPJ) and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

== History ==

=== Founding (1984) ===

Corporació de Plàstics Jala was spun off from [[Grup Rojo]] in 1984 as a dedicated high-performance plastics subsidiary. The new company was created to separate engineering plastics from Grup Rojo's broader oxo alcohol, plasticizer, and polyethylene business, allowing CPJ to focus on specialty polymers for aerospace, electronics, chemical processing, and industrial applications.

The company began as a small PTFE processing business serving the industrial and chemical-seals market. Its early success came from supplying gasket, lining, and valve-seat materials to the Balboan chemical industry, especially users of [[CIEA]]'s refinery system and related downstream plants at [[Badia Curta]]. The company name refers to the [[Jala]] region, where the industrial complex is located.

=== Expansion into advanced polymers (1990s) ===

During the 1990s, CPJ expanded into a broader range of high-performance polymers, adding '''PEEK''' and '''PAI''' production for aerospace and electronics customers, followed by '''PBI''' and '''ECTFE''' for chemical-processing and high-corrosion applications. The company invested heavily in polymerisation, compounding, and precision machining capacity to support these grades, which require tight process control and specialized raw-material handling.

The establishment of the [[BTPMEU]] and the growth of Balboa's export industries gave CPJ access to nearby regional markets, while the negative tariff made exports more competitive. By the end of the decade, the company had become the country's principal producer of high-performance fluoropolymers and one of the leading suppliers of engineering plastics in the region.

=== Listing and growth (2001–present) ===

CPJ was listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] in 2001. The listing funded the expansion of its Jala province complex, including new PTFE and PEEK lines, an ECTFE fluorination unit, and a precision-moulding facility for finished polymer components. The [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB) acquired a 6 per cent stake at the time of the listing, and the [[Balboa Pension Fund]] acquired a 4 per cent stake.

In the 2010s and 2020s, CPJ expanded further into aerospace-grade polymers, semiconductor-process components, and corrosion-resistant linings for chemical and energy customers. The company also became an important supplier to Balboa's domestic medical-device and industrial-equipment sectors.

== Products ==

CPJ's product portfolio consists of six core high-performance polymers:

* '''PEEK''' (polyether ether ketone): Aerospace, semiconductor, and high-temperature industrial applications.
* '''PAI''' (polyamide-imide): Bearings, seals, insulating components, and high-stress engineering parts.
* '''PBI''' (polybenzimidazole): High-temperature insulation and protective components.
* '''ECTFE''' (ethylene chlorotrifluoroethylene): Chemical linings, tubing, and corrosion-resistant films.
* '''PI''' (polyimide): Electronics, aerospace, and flexible-circuit applications.
* '''PTFE''' (polytetrafluoroethylene): Seals, gaskets, coatings, and chemical-processing components.

The company also provides compounding, machining, and custom part fabrication services for industrial customers.

== Operations ==

* '''Headquarters''': 112 Carrer 5è, Zone 2, [[Sant Bart]]
* '''Main complex''': [[Jala]] province — polymerisation, fluorination, compounding, machining, and precision moulding facilities
* '''Employees''': approximately 2,600 (2026)
* '''Exports''': Illypnia, [[Balisca]], [[Okaiken]], [[Tapuya]], and [[Sanrobonia]]

CPJ's Jala complex is the company's only major production site, allowing it to maintain tight process integration across its engineering plastic lines. The site is positioned to serve both domestic customers and export markets through Balboa's logistics network.

== Ownership ==

CPJ is publicly traded on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]]. The ownership structure reflects the company's origin as a spin-off from Grup Rojo:

* '''[[Grup Rojo]]''': 22% — retained stake after the spin-off
* '''[[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FIDB)''': 6% — strategic domestic institutional stake
* '''[[Balboa Pension Fund]] (BPF)''': 4% — institutional anchor investor
* '''Public float''': approximately 68% — held by institutional and retail investors

== Competition ==

CPJ competes with [[Polímers de Balboa]] in industrial plastics, but its core focus is much narrower and more specialised: high-performance polymers rather than commodity resins. It also competes with imported engineering plastics from Illypnia and Balisca, particularly in aerospace and electronics applications.

